Description: When a command fails, Kintsu offers to hand it to your AI agent, in the shell
 Any provider, your own key. Kintsu hooks your shell (zsh, bash, fish). After
 a failed command it prints one bubble: what happened, a fix when a rule knows
 one, and the words to ask your models or hand the case to your coding agent,
 in your own terminal. Rules work with no configuration and nothing leaves the
 machine. Add the hook yourself: eval "$(kintsu init zsh)" in ~/.zshrc,
 eval "$(kintsu init bash)" in ~/.bashrc, or kintsu init fish | source in
 ~/.config/fish/config.fish.
